  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let \\(f:(0,2)\\cup(4,6)\\to\\mathbb R\\) be a differentiable function. Suppose also that \\(f'(x)=1\\) for all \\(x\\in(0,2)\\cup(4,6)\\). Which of the following is ALWAYS true?",
  "options": {
    "A": "\\(f\\) is increasing",
    "B": "\\(f\\) is one-to-one",
    "C": "\\(f(x)=x\\) for all \\(x\\in(0,2)\\cup(4,6)\\)",
    "D": "\\(f(5.5)-f(4.5)=f(1.5)-f(0.5)\\)"
  },
  "answer": "D",
